{"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "schema", "document", "Document"], "kwargs": {"metadata": {"source": "data\\documents\\csv\\QA-Kaggle-dataset-2024_utf8.csv", "filename": "QA-Kaggle-dataset-2024_utf8.csv", "filepath": "data\\documents\\csv\\QA-Kaggle-dataset-2024_utf8.csv", "page": 2, "title": "QA-Kaggle-dataset-2024_utf8.csv", "year": "2024", "row": 1}, "page_content": "\ufeffWhat is psoriasis and what are its common symptoms?: What are the treatment modalities for acne?\nPsoriasis is a chronic autoimmune condition that results in the overproduction of skin cells. This overproduction leads to patches of thick, red skin covered with silvery scales. Common symptoms include red patches of skin covered with thick, silvery scales, small scaling spots (commonly seen in children), dry and cracked skin that may bleed, itching, burning, or soreness, thickened, pitted, or ridged nails, and swollen and stiff joints.: Acne treatment depends on the severity of the condition. Mild acne can often be managed with over-the-counter products containing ingredients like benzoyl peroxide or salicylic acid. For moderate to severe acne, prescription medications may be necessary. These can include topical treatments such as retinoids and antibiotics, or oral medications like antibiotics, combined oral contraceptives, anti-androgen agents, or isotretinoin. In some cases, therapies such as lasers and photodynamic therapy, chemical peels, or extraction of whiteheads and blackheads may be recommended.", "type": "Document"}}